1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,776
Sleep is an active process during which the brain sorts

2
00:00:03,776 --> 00:00:07,209
memories and clears waste built up during the day.

3
00:00:07,259 --> 00:00:11,032
The night is split into repeating cycles of light sleep

4
00:00:11,032 --> 00:00:15,559
Deep sleep and dream sleep, each doing different work for the body

5
00:00:15,609 --> 00:00:19,206
Going without enough sleep makes it harder to concentrate

6
00:00:19,206 --> 00:00:23,182
Remember new facts and react quickly to what happens around you

7
00:00:23,232 --> 00:00:26,688
Over months and years, regular short sleep is linked

8
00:00:26,688 --> 00:00:30,077
With higher risks of heart problems and weight gain

9
00:00:30,127 --> 00:00:34,102
Keeping the same bedtime and wake-up time, even on weekends

10
00:00:34,102 --> 00:00:37,336
Helps the body clock settle into a steady rhythm

11
00:00:37,386 --> 00:00:41,024
Bright screens late in the evening can delay sleepiness

12
00:00:41,024 --> 00:00:44,595
Because light tells the brain that it is still daytime

13
00:00:44,645 --> 00:00:48,866
To build a better routine, first fix your wake-up time, then

14
00:00:48,866 --> 00:00:52,945
dim the lights early, and finally keep screens out of bed.

15
00:00:52,995 --> 00:00:58,054
Sleep problems that last for weeks, such as loud snoring with daytime exhaustion

16
00:00:58,054 --> 00:01:00,205
Are worth discussing with a doctor

